  "interpretation": "Hargreaves and Penman\u2013Monteith ET0 agree within a few percent, and matched-day ECOSTRESS ratios equal the monthly ones, so neither ET0 nor clear-sky sampling explains the gap. The claypan-limited storage agrees better than the full profile with all three independent observations (ECOSTRESS level, SMAP timing, county yield swings) but the model still over-estimates ECOSTRESS crop water use. Likely remaining causes: no runoff (K-State/USDA-ARS: only ~25% of fallow-season rain is stored), a seasonal-average Kc instead of stage curves, ECOSTRESS 70 m / overpass-time sampling, and county yields mixing irrigated fields. The model is exploratory."
